<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32307" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oenanthē</span></b> , ēs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνάνθη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The grape of the wild vine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				28, 61, § 132</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A thorny plant</i>, <i>pimpinella-like
				dropwort</i>: Oenanthe pimpinelloides, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 21,
				24, 95, § 167</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A bird</i>, <i>called also</i> parra,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				10, 29, 45, § 87</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>Œnanthe</i>, <i>mother of
				Ptolemy Epiphanes</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 30,
				3, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>